  "result": "I wrote the concept body and its three witnesses, and the gate returned **OK** on the first run (1 of 6 used).\n\n**The body:** it compares the cosine of the angle between the road user's heading and the carrier's direction against `-cos_tol`. That cosine is the dot product of the two vectors. Core already returns both vectors normalised, so the body takes their x and y components, adds `hx·dx + hy·dy`, and holds when the sum is strictly below `-cos_tol`. If either vector is missing, or the carrier has no designated direction, the result is unknown, as the contract says. The contract left no choices open, so I declared no narrowings.\n\n**The witnesses:**\n- **Setup:** a one-way roadway (region 100) with designated direction east, and a car (track 1) parked inside it. The car is at rest so that only the direction it points matters.\n- **Instance:** `cos_tol` is set to 9/10, so a heading within about 26° of exactly opposed counts as against.\n- **holds:** the car points west (cosine −1), giving compliant.\n- **fails:** the car points east (cosine +1), giving violated.\n- **blind:** the same scene as holds, with `kin.heading` declared absent, giving unknown.\n\nThe record needed no changes and I found no faulty dependency, so I didn't write a `dependency_defect.json`. `task_result.md` is in the working directory.\n\nFiles changed:\n- `library/TrafficSpec/Concepts/lane/facing_against_direction.lean`\n- `library/TrafficSpecWitness/Concepts/lane/facing_against_direction.lean`",
